[narrator · region 9]
At three o'clock the door of SUDS opens and a woman comes in
with a mop and a yellow bucket on wheels. Fifties, a cardigan
over a tabard that says SUDS, a name badge that says MARA,
reading glasses on a cord. She nods at the three of them the way
you nod at regulars and starts mopping by the door. A minute
later a man in a quilted jacket comes in after her with a
clipboard and a torch and begins going along the row of washers,
opening each little coin box, peering in, writing something
down.

