[narrator · region 9]
They talk. The attendant mops her way round the bench and back,
and asks the questions anyone asks a stranger at three in the
morning: work, family, whether they've eaten, whether it's still
raining. The landlord's man goes along the dryers with his torch
and his clipboard, slowly, opening every coin box, and starts
again at the first one when he reaches the end. Pip answers
everything with something nobody could have guessed and
something nobody could use. Reeve answers short, and late, and
sideways. Mori answers like Mori, warm and too long, and every
few minutes he says something a beat after Reeve that is almost
what Reeve said.

